Info_BMP_IMG_1,                     "All Windows bitmaps (BMP) can be directly read by MiraMon through \"File | Open raster\" indicating the BMP extension.\n\n"
Info_BMP_IMG_2,                     "If afterwards you wish to convert the file to IMG, save it through \"File | Save as IMG\" selecting the option \"Full raster\"."
Info_IDRISI_IMG_1,                  "All Idrisi IMG files being binary and non packed can be directly read by MiraMon through  \"File | Open raster\".\n\n"
Info_IDRISI_IMG_2,                  "If the file is ASCII or packed, simply convert it to binary non packed through the Idrisi CONVERT application (ASCII files can also be imported directly from MiraMon through \"File | Import | Rasters | ASCII->IMG\")."
Info_TOPSHP,                        "To convert MiraMon structured vector files to Shapefiles, export them to E00 (\"File | PNT, ARC/NOD, POL -> E00\") and:\n\tFrom ArcView 3, execute \"Import\" and \"Theme | Convert to Shapefile\"."
Info_TOPSHPExtra,				"\n\tFrom ArcView 8, execute, from \"ArcToolBox\", \"Import to coverage | Import from interchange file\" and \"Export from coverage | Export to shapefile\"."
Info_IDRISI_TOPMM,                  "To convert any Idrisi VEC file to a MiraMon topologically structured vector, use the \"Edit | Build topology\" tools."
Info_IDRISI_VEC,                    "All Idrisi VEC files being ASCII can be directly read by MiraMon through  \"File | Open Non-structured vector\".\n\nIf the VEC file is binary, simply convert it to ASCII through the Idrisi \"CONVERT V\" application."
Info_IMG_BMP,                       "To save an IMG file or RGB composite as a Windows bitmap, load it into MiraMon through  \"File | Open raster\" or \"File | Open RGB->24-bit\" and execute \"File | Save as BMP\"."
Info_IMG_IDRISI,                    "All MiraMon IMG files being non compressed nor bit nor long are directly compatible with Idrisi.\n\nTo convert bit, long or compressed files to Idrisi execute \"Tools | File maintenance | Raster conversion and compression/uncompression\"."
Info_TOPMM_IDRISI_1,                "To convert MiraMon topologically structured vectors to Idrisi VEC files, load them into MiraMon (\"File | Open structured vector\"), select all entities (\"Information | Query by attributes\", ID_GRAFIC>=0) "
Info_TOPMM_IDRISI_2,                "and save the selection as a VEC file.\n\nTo convert PNT->VEC and ARC->VEC you can also use the \"Points\" and \"Arcs/Nodes\" options from the \"Edit | Build topology\" menu."
Info_VEC_IDRISI_1,                  "All MiraMon VEC files are directly compatible with Idrisi, except those having attributes of type \"string\" and those \"integer\" ranging outside [-32768,32767]; "
Info_VEC_IDRISI_2,                  "in these cases, attributes should be reclassified to some of the types supported by Idrisi (short integer or real)."

