No_refresc_periodic_Explica_1,	"There are no layers with periodic refresh.\n\nFor GPS tracking you do not need to do nothing because it is done automatically by the GPSMM application. To define a periodic refresh under other circumstances include, in the desired [VECTOR_#] section of the "
No_refresc_periodic_Explica_2,	"MiraMon Map (MMM) file, the key \"RefrescPeriodic=nnnnnn\" where nnnnnn is the refresh time in milliseconds.\n\nThis will refresh symbolization, so you can change database contents from a remote system and view changes in MiraMon in real time.\n\n"
No_refresc_periodic_Explica_3,	"For applications needing to refresh the graphical entities themselves (because they are changing according to external inputs), add an additional key \"TipusRefrescPeriodic=1\"."
Refresc_periodic_Explica_1,	"To define a periodic refresh include, in the desired [VECTOR_#] section of the MiraMon Map (MMM) file, the key \"RefrescPeriodic=nnnnnn\" where nnnnnn is the refresh time in milliseconds.\n\nThis will refresh symbolization, so you can change database "
Refresc_periodic_Explica_2,	"contents from a remote system and view changes in MiraMon in real time.\n\nFor applications needing to refresh the graphical entities themselves (because they are changing according to external inputs), add an additional key \"TipusRefrescPeriodic=1\"."
Refresc_periodic_Explica_3,	"\n\nFor GPS tracking  it is only necessary to call the GPSMM application.\n\nFor tracking of selected objects, you need to select this option in the window of refresh and tracking and you also need to indicate the time of refresh in milliseconds, "
Refresc_periodic_Explica_4,	"then, when you select objects, by attribute and/or interactively (in this case the layer must have an identity identifier), the objects will remain visible on the screen."
Cal_IdEntitat_t_ppal_fitxer_s_sel_interac,   "When the layer is refreshed, the main table of the file '%s' must have a field defined as an entity identifier to keep the interactive selection."

