Arcs_ciclats_no_suporten_1, "When an arc layer provides arcs for cycling a polygon layer, its graphic and/or alphanumeric (attributes) editing must be done by digitizing the associated polygon layer.\n\nIf you only want to make changes "
Arcs_ciclats_no_suporten_2, "to the attributes you can do it from \"Edit | Edit vector attributes\" (Shift+F2).\n\nIf you really need a full edit (geometry, topology and attributes) of this arc layer, explicitly unlink all its polygon "
Arcs_ciclats_no_suporten_2_i_mig, "layers until the number of cycled layers is zero through \"Presentation | Technical aspects\" in the Universal Geospatial Metadata Manager (GeM+)."
Arcs_ciclats_no_suporten_3, " If you want to previously save these polygon layers you can execute \"Tools | File Maintenance | Emancipate polygons from arcs\"; "
Arcs_ciclats_no_suporten_4, "you may also generate labels with the thematic attributes to be transferred to the new polygons with \"Automatic label generation...\", in the same menu."
Eliminar_Arcs_NO_CICLAR_MAI_1,	"This layer contains arcs (other than pending arcs created by the user during a polygons' digitizing session) that are not involved in cycling the polygons of the layer."
Eliminar_Arcs_NO_CICLAR_MAI_2,	"They probably came from the fact that the arcs file had been involved in cycling other layers of polygons.\n\nIf you want to delete them, please press \"Yes\"."

